Even one 256-entry bank per recipe costs 4352, exceeding the available4184 by 168; this fixed-bank policy cannot meet the reference without additional base savings.

## Scope and limitations
- Domain corrected to width/depth1..16 with min(width,depth)<=8:192pairs,768oriented plans. Previous128-pair report preserved separately.
- Separate family-proportion candidate uses width families1/3/7 and depth families1/2/3 via sourceModel for BOTH visual slicing and native collision. Original study remains unchanged.
- Shared garment is generated with twoSided:true for the open altar, including reverse drape faces.
- Face complexity counts explicitly authored UV face records, including interior closure faces; no occlusion-based culling assumed. Every quad is two triangles. These are measurements, not gate changes.
- Fixed bank uses index = low + 16*high + 256*page. Append page values without reordering low/high/page values or existing codebook entries. This preserves existing numeric mappings; a schema expansion still requires validation and must not renumber the palette.
- Recount uses capCuts:true and continuous shaft UVs in the stabilized cell study. Baseline reports are preserved separately.
- Packing enumerates all three-property products with each cardinality1..16, retaining recipe in its own ID and logical facing in the packed codebook, not as a fourth independent axis.
- Canonical object keys remove insertion-order-only distinctions in source cubes; raw-key-order counts are reported alongside for comparison with the earlier 1,160-profile measurement.
- Recipe identity is retained even when interior cells have the same visible material. Logical facing is retained in the second count, even for symmetric or hidden cloth.
- Only actually co-occurring pedestal profile, contour, textile center role and facing are enumerated across all 768 permitted oriented assemblies.
- Garment is generated from the real shared generator with fixed edges. Face material slots are replaced by their actual texture keys; unused material bindings do not inflate signatures.
- Collision is the existing nativeBoxes study output, not a new collision design. Cubes are hashed canonically as sorted multisets; arrays inside cubes retain order.
- This measures structural-plus-garment composition keys, not a validated rendered integration. Existing wooden top reaches16 and linen occupies15.91..16: implement an explicit covered-top clipping/removal policy before rendering. Such changes can alter profile counts.
- Garment defaults use stoneEdge8.28/cornerEnd8.34, as shared generator; pedestal-specific attachment fit and cube/block limits require validation.
- The structural wood is deliberately not culled behind cloth. Removing hidden wooden faces could reduce counts, but is not assumed.
- These are exact construction-codebook entry counts, not padded declared-state totals, theoretical minima, or approved runtime schemas. No catalog/runtime/world changes.

Run: node --experimental-strip-types tools/audit-pedestal-family-budget.mjs
